# Provenance
- Code: `sweep.py` (repo root). Job: `ht-resource run local-compute --cwd /hutian/repo -- python3 -u sweep.py`, job ref job-325ee65149 (final run, two-point fits allowed; earlier job-d2a4c8de6c added n_values_used and r_squared to fits.csv; first run job-b28af73dd4), exit 0, printed "HUTIAN_WAKE: sweep done".
- mpmath 1.4.1 (pip install mpmath numpy; numpy 2.4.6); references from `mpmath.quad(f,[0,1])` at mp.dps=40 -> `reference.csv`.
- Panels: n = 2^k panels on [0,1], width 1/n. Trapezoid: one interval per panel. Simpson: each panel is one Simpson rule on [a,a+h] with its midpoint (2n subintervals total). Gauss4: 4-node Gauss-Legendre per panel.
- Rules evaluated in float64; error = |float64 value (exact as mpf) - 40-digit reference|, written with 7 significant digits (`abs_error`); `value` column holds the full float64 repr.
- Fits: least squares of ln(error) vs ln(n) over rows with error > 1e-14; order = -slope; `n_points_above_1e-14` in fits.csv; at least 2 distinct n are needed. Gauss4 on exp(-x^2) has only 2 such points (n=2,4): its order is a two-point slope, with no residual degrees of freedom (R^2 = nan), so it is not a robust asymptotic estimate.
- Rule names in errors.csv `rule`: trapezoid (composite trapezoid), simpson (composite Simpson), gauss4 (4-node Gauss-Legendre panels). `function` values: `exp(-x^2)`, `x^(1/3)`. `abs_error` is parseable scientific notation.
